    "created_at": "2016-08-17T15:16:19Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-08-17T15:16:19Z",
    "body": "Yes, that's not meant to override the CSS definition. The main difference between the canvas and CSS cases is that in the CSS case, the filter can be applied to the content once it finishes loading, but in the canvas case each drawing operation is synchronous, so we can't go back and retroactively apply the filter to previous draw operations once the filter is loaded. \n",
